hadiths[17]{hadithnumber,text}:
"902","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` ﻿ the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Medina is a sanctuary from here (Mount ‘Ir) to there (Thawr); its trees should not be cut, nor should any oppression or innovation be committed here. Whoever invents any act of oppression or innovation here, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people (and in one narration: whoever gives shelter to an innovator, upon him as well)."""
"903","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The land between the two rocky boundaries of Madinah has been declared a sanctuary by my tongue."" (Further) he says that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) went to the tribe of Banu Harithah and said: ""I think you have gone outside the sanctuary."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) looked around and said: ""No! You are within the sanctuary."""
"904","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: We have nothing except the Book of Allah and this scroll which has been transmitted from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (It also contains this subject): ""From the mountain of 'Ayr in Madinah to such-and-such place (Thawr) is a sanctuary (Haram). Whoever introduces an innovation (bid'ah) here, acts upon it, or gives refuge to an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither any voluntary worship nor any obligatory worship will be accepted from him."" And he said: ""The covenant of any one Muslim is sufficient among you; then whoever breaks the covenant of any Muslim, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither any voluntary worship nor any obligatory worship will be accepted from him. And whoever (a slave) leaves his master and, without his permission, takes another as master, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither any voluntary worship nor any obligatory worship will be accepted from him."""
"905","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (before migration): ""I have been commanded to go to a town which will overcome all other towns. It is called 'Yathrib', and it is Madinah. It expels evil people just as a furnace removes impurities from iron."""
"906","Sayyiduna Abu Humayd Sa‘idi (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we returned from Tabuk with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). When we approached near Madinah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This is 'Taba'."" (i.e., he referred to Madinah as 'Taba')."
"907","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""(Near the Day of Judgment, a time will come when) people will leave Madinah in a very good condition, and none will remain there except wild animals, birds, and beasts. The last two shepherds from the tribe of Muzaina will come to Madinah to drive away their goats, and they will find Madinah filled with wild animals and beasts. When they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada', they will fall down on their faces (i.e., they will die and the Hour will be established)."""
"908","Sufyan bin Abu Zuhair (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""(In the future) Yemen will be conquered, and there will be some people who will drive their mounts fast and will take their families and those who obey them from Madinah to Yemen, even though Madinah would be better for them if they understood. And Sham will be conquered, and there will be some people who will drive their mounts fast and will take their families and those who obey them from Madinah to Sham, even though Madinah would be better for them if they understood. And Iraq will be conquered, and there will be some people who will drive their mounts fast and will take their families and those who obey them from Madinah to Iraq, even though Madinah would be better for them if they understood."""
"909","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Iman (faith) will gather towards Madinah just as a snake gathers towards its hole."""
"910","The conqueror of Persia and Iran, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “Whoever deceives the people of Madinah will dissolve just as salt dissolves in water.”"
"911","Narrated Usama (may Allah be pleased with him): (One day) the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) climbed one of the hills of Madinah and said: ""Do you see what I am seeing? Indeed, I see the places where trials will descend among your houses (they will be so many) like the drops of a heavy rain."""
"912","`Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The awe of the Messiah Dajjal will not enter Madinah. At that time, Madinah will have seven gates, and at each gate there will be two angels (standing guard)."""
"913","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Angels will guard the gates of Madinah; neither the plague will enter there nor will the Dajjal be able to enter Madinah."""
"914","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""The Dajjal will certainly trample every city in the world except Makkah and Madinah. On every path to these two, angels will stand in rows as guards. Then Madinah will shake its people three times with great force, and Allah will expel every disbeliever and hypocrite (who will be present in Madinah at that time)."""
"915","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) narrated to us a very long story about the Dajjal. Among the things he (peace be upon him) told us was this: “The Dajjal will come and stop at the salty barren land near Madinah, but entering Madinah will be forbidden for him. At that time, a man who will be the best and most righteous among the people will go to the Dajjal and say, ‘I bear witness that you are the same Dajjal about whom the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) has informed us in the hadith.’ The Dajjal will then say to the people, ‘Tell me! If I kill this man and then bring him back to life, will you still doubt my matter?’ The people will reply, ‘No.’ So the Dajjal will first kill this righteous man and then bring him back to life. When the righteous man is brought back to life, he will say, ‘By Allah! Now I am even more certain that you are indeed the Dajjal.’ Then the Dajjal will try to kill this righteous man again, but he will not be able to do so.”"
"916","Narrated Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and pledged allegiance to him for Islam. Then the next day he came suffering from fever and said, ""Take back your pledge."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused three times. Then he said: ""Medina is like a furnace; it removes impurities and retains what is good and pure."""
"917","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Grant twice the blessings in Madinah as You have placed in Makkah."""
"918","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) migrated to Madinah, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with them) were afflicted with fever. The condition of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was that when he would get a fever, he would say: “Every person wakes up in his own house in the morning, and (he does not know that) death is closer to him than the strap of his sandal.” And the condition of Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was that when he would get a fever, he would raise his voice and say: “Oh, if only I knew whether I would ever again spend a night in a valley surrounded by Idhkhir and Jalil (types of grass), and whether I would ever reach the springs of Majannah, and whether I would ever see Shamah and Tufail (names of mountains) again?” (Then he would also supplicate:) “O Allah! Curse Shaybah bin Rabi’ah, Utbah bin Rabi’ah, and Umayyah bin Khalaf, just as they expelled us from our homeland (Makkah) to a land of epidemic (Madinah).” Upon hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) supplicated: “O Allah! Instill the love of Madinah in our hearts as You have instilled the love of Makkah, or even more than that. O Allah! Bless our Sa’ and our Mudd, and make the climate of Madinah suitable for us, and transfer its fever to (the area of) Juhfah (where the polytheists reside).” (Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her) says: When we came to Madinah, it was the most epidemic-ridden land of Allah. She also says: At that time, foul-smelling water used to flow in the valley of Bathan."
